{"run_id": "20260814T133731-hepkg-48443", "qid": "gen-retrieval-58a054cb", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "9f0ca51b332d", "git_sha": "feb9060-dirty", "question": "Which analyses used the generator JETSET 7.408 hadronization/interface program?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "hard", "answer": {"text": "The analysis in the paper with arXiv ID 2009.14537 used the generator JETSET 7.408 hadronization/interface program. This paper focuses on the following aspects:\n\n- **Background Estimation Methods**:\n  - Background-only profile-likelihood fit normalization of mixed-data sample.\n  - Data-driven mixed-data sample method for combinatorial background estimation.\n\n- **Event Regions**:\n  - Baseline preselection common to all signal regions.\n  - Particle-level fiducial region for cross-section measurement.\n  - ll+p proton-tagged signal region.\n\n- **Benchmark**:\n  - SuperChic 4 fiducial cross-section prediction with fully kinematically dependent S_surv.\n\n- **Selection Requirements**:\n  - Acoplanarity \\( A_φ^{ℓℓ} = 1-|Δφ_ℓℓ|/π < 0.01 \\).\n  - Additional Medium identification requirement.\n  - Both leptons matched to the leptons that triggered the event.\n  - Electrons sharing an inner-detector track with a muon are discarded (overlap removal).\n  - Exactly two same-flavor, opposite-charge leptons (e+e- or μ+μ-).\n  - Fiducial (particle-level) acceptance restricted to \\( ξ_AFP, ξ_ℓℓ \\) in [0.035,0.08].\n  - Isolation requirements.\n  - Kinematic matching \\( |ξ_AFP - ξ_ℓℓ| < 0.005 \\) on at least one AFP side.\n  - LooseAndBLayer identification criterion.\n  - Medium identification criterion.\n  - Veto on additional tracks with \\( ΔR(track,ℓ) > 0.01 \\) for both leptons and \\( |z0^track - z0^ℓℓ| < 0.5 \\) mm.\n  - Per-side/per-station acceptance thresholds after alignment corrections.\n  - Proton candidate required to have an associated track in both near and far AFP stations.\n  - Track reconstructed from clusters in at least two AFP tracker planes.\n  - When multiple proton candidates exist on the same AFP side, the candidate with \\( ξ_AFP \\) closest to \\( ξ_ℓℓ \\) is designated.\n  - \\( m_ℓℓ > 20 \\) GeV and \\( m_ℓℓ \\) not in [70,105] GeV.\n  - \\( pT > 14 \\) GeV at trigger level.\n\nThis analysis is part of a detailed study involving the use of JETSET 7.408 for hadronization and interface purposes.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2001.06899", "2004.01678", "2004.04545", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2008.05928", "2009.04363", "2009.14537", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2012.01581", "2012.03799", "2012.08600", "2102.01444", "2103.04956", "2103.06956", "2106.01676", "2106.14246", "2107.12553", "2109.13808", "2110.11231", "2111.08340", "2112.03161", "2201.11585", "2202.08676", "2205.05120", "2206.09466", "2207.00348", "2208.12095", "2209.07327", "2211.08028", "2302.05225", "2303.15340", "2304.08962", "2307.01094", "2308.02285", "2309.14442", "2312.04450", "2401.05299", "2401.07090", "2402.08486", "2403.01556", "2404.06204", "2405.18661", "2407.10549", "2408.03744", "2503.19420", "2504.13081", "2506.13565", "2508.13900", "2509.22535", "2510.07527", "2511.11853", "2602.18611", "2604.21670", "2604.27044", "2605.14245"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "search", "args": {"text": "JETSET 7.408", "kind": "generator"}, "rows": 17, "error": null, "seconds": 0.107}, {"round": 2, "tool": "count", "args": {"predicate": "sample_uses_generator", "object_set": "set_1"}, "rows": 1, "error": null, "seconds": 0.064}, {"round": 3, "tool": "count", "args": {"predicate": "sample_uses_generator", "object_ids": ["hepkg:generator:jetset7.408"]}, "rows": 1, "error": null, "seconds": 0.005}, {"round": 4, "tool": "papers_of", "args": {"entity_ids": ["hepkg:generator:jetset7.408"]}, "rows": 1, "error": null, "seconds": 0.008}, {"round": 5, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2009.14537"]}, "rows": 124, "error": null, "seconds": 0.286}], "sets": {"set_1"