{"run_id": "20260814T133731-hepkg-48443", "qid": "gen-retrieval-6002e716", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "9f0ca51b332d", "git_sha": "feb9060-dirty", "question": "Which analyses define the region On-shell WZ selection signal regions (SR^WZ)?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "hard", "answer": {"text": "The following analyses define the region \"On-shell WZ selection signal regions (SR^WZ)\":\n\n1. **Paper:** \"Measurement of the inclusive and differential ${\\mathup{{{W}}}}{\\mathup{{{Z}}}}$ production cross sections, polarization angles, and triple gauge couplings in ${\\mathup{{{p}}}}{\\mathup{{{p}}}}$ collisions at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\,\\text{Te\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$\" (arXiv: 2110.11231)\n2. **Paper:** \"Measurements of the Higgs boson production cross section and couplings in the $W$ boson pair decay channel in proton-proton collisions at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\,\\text{Te\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$\" (arXiv: 2206.09466)\n3. **Paper:** \"Measurements of the production cross-sections of a Higgs boson in association with a vector boson and decaying into $WW^{*}$ with the ATLAS detector at $\\sqrt{s}=13$ TeV\" (arXiv: 2503.19420)\n\nThese papers each define the region \"On-shell WZ selection signal regions (SR^WZ)\" in their respective analyses.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.01678", "2007.02873", "2009.04363", "2009.14537", "2011.07812", "2012.01581", "2103.04956", "2106.01676", "2106.14246", "2107.12553", "2109.13808", "2110.11231", "2111.08340", "2201.11585", "2205.05120", "2206.09466", "2209.07327", "2304.08962", "2308.02285", "2312.04450", "2401.05299", "2402.08486", "2404.06204", "2408.03744", "2503.19420", "2508.13900", "2509.22535", "2510.07527", "2602.18611", "2604.21670"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "search", "args": {"text": "On-shell WZ selection signal regions (SR^WZ)", "kind": "event_region"}, "rows": 60, "error": null, "seconds": 0.225}, {"round": 2, "tool": "subjects_of", "args": {"predicate": "resu